From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:59:58 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 069/106] arm64: dts: exynos7570: j4lte: boot the root
 filesystem from USERDATA

The system partition is too small for a desktop. The installed system now
lives on a journaled ext4 on USERDATA; SYSTEM stays as it was for the
downstream kernel.

Signed-off-by: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d4c13b81e999467a41e52b3b3e44b28e36843396)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
index 0f08aae3e..a49c7e1ad 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ chosen {
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges;
 
-		bootargs = "console=tty0 ignore_loglevel clk_ignore_unused regulator_ignore_unused";
+		bootargs = "console=tty0 ignore_loglevel clk_ignore_unused regulator_ignore_unused root=/dev/mmcblk0p25 rootfstype=ext4";
 
 		/* Set up by the bootloader (uniLoader), scanned out by DECON */
 		framebuffer0: framebuffer@67000000 {
